#%PAM-1.0
# LionOS greeter PAM stack.
#
# Common Debian/Ubuntu stacks (pam_unix/sssd, pam_faildelay, pam_systemd,
# pam_env, limits, etc.) all come from the common-* includes. Adjust
# locally if LionOS ships a different distro base.
#
# Module order:
#   1. pam_nologin (auth)        — hard-fail if /etc/nologin exists.
#   2. common-auth                — actual password check (pam_unix, etc.)
#   3. pam_nologin (account)     — same gate, account phase.
#   4. common-account            — expiry / lockout checks.
#   5. pam_loginuid (session)    — set the audit loginuid.
#   6. common-session             — pam_systemd registers a logind session
#                                  (XDG_SESSION_ID, XDG_RUNTIME_DIR, ...)
#   7. pam_keyinit force revoke   — per-user session keyring.
#
# `pam_faildelay` is pulled in via `common-auth` and stretches the
# response time of failed logins so timing attacks cannot distinguish
# "user not found" from "wrong password". The lion-greeter daemon
# independently enforces a 600ms minimum-failure-latency and a per-user
# doubling throttle (see src/throttle.rs) — these stack with PAM's own
# delay, they don't replace it.
auth      requisite  pam_nologin.so
@include common-auth
account   required   pam_nologin.so
@include common-account
session   required   pam_loginuid.so
@include common-session
session   optional   pam_keyinit.so force revoke
